COMMERCIAL S11 RUNTIME HEALTH AND IN-FLIGHT POLLER DIAGNOSIS

Status: ROOT_CAUSE_CONFIRMED; S11_DISABLED; SOURCE_RUNTIME_RESTORED

The r5 deployment installed the exact frozen Application and Control releases,
applied the additive S11 migration with the established PostgreSQL administrator
ingress and kept the feature disabled. The first post-restart runtime health
gate then failed closed. Automatic rollback restored the source Application,
Control, package, units and configuration. S11 tables remain preserved with the
feature disabled and with zero sessions and zero product events.

The immediate health failure is not a poller, lease, provider, moderation or
release-binding failure. Privacy-safe aggregate inspection proves one live,
release-bound poller, a future lease, a recent successful poll, a green provider,
zero pending moderation and zero stuck restrictions. The failing condition is
the pre-existing Community 24-hour latency SLO: six DIRECT samples include an
update backlog processed after earlier runtime interruption, including values at
the existing 300-second cap. No sample, KPI or acquisition baseline is changed.

The rollback readiness check exposed a separate controller defect. The poller
sets `BOT_UPDATE_NOT_RECEIVED` while a bounded Telegram long-poll is in flight,
then writes `BOT_EVENT_PATH_GREEN` after the successful response. Requiring the
latter exact value at every instant can reject a healthy live poller. The r6
gate accepts the in-flight code only when all independent fences are also true:
the exact release, one non-null owner, a future lease and a successful poll in
the preceding 90 seconds. All error codes remain rejected.

Bounded correction:
- add an exact read-only Community latency SLO gate to source preflight so the
  current red condition stops before backup and deployment mutation;
- align the controller readiness query with the Application poller health
  contract for the strictly fenced in-flight long-poll state;
- retain all latency evidence and the real-acquisition baseline unchanged;
- do not use a manual Telegram message to manufacture health;
- do not change the 1s/2s/5s SLO thresholds or the five-sample minimum;
- keep S11 OFF until the unchanged rolling window becomes GREEN naturally.

Retry contract:
- merge and freeze the r6 controller through the normal CI and same-SHA review;
- run r6 preflight read-only; RED must be `S11_COMMUNITY_LATENCY_SLO_RED` while
  the window is degraded;
- make no new deployment attempt until both S9 and S10 health are GREEN;
- then use a fresh timestamped predeploy backup and the exact r6 freeze.

Adult media, real AVS, payment, external publishing, Community user-content
publishing, Controlled Beta and production remain closed.
